Ladybird clamps a table’s specified height by its max-height, raises it
to its min-height, and makes that the table grid’s minimum block size.

Blink computes the table’s block size with ComputeBlockSizeForFragment()
in TableLayoutAlgorithm, which applies min-height and max-height, and
distributes it to the sections when it exceeds their minimum. Gecko’s
nsTableFrame::CalcBorderBoxBSize() applies ApplyMinMaxBSize() to it.
WebKit’s RenderTable::layout() clamps the computed height by max-height
and then raises it to min-height before distributing the extra height.
